  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (+)-Iridodial lactol may interact with HaCaT through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links (+)-Iridodial lactol to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by Oleamide, and subsequently targets HaCaT. The second pathway connects (+)-Iridodial lactol to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is targeted by a compound related to 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which also targets HaCaT. The third pathway shows that (+)-Iridodial lactol targets Ataxin-2, which is targeted by Plantago seed, and thus also targets HaCaT. These findings collectively indicate that (+)-Iridodial lactol may exert its effects on HaCaT through different molecular mechanisms, potentially involving proteasome regulation and protein targeting. The evidence is consistent with a role for (+)-Iridodial lactol in modulating HaCaT through these indirect pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated."
